One fleet host degraded for weeks while nothing watched it: the macOS file-event daemon grew to an 86 GB footprint, a one-off job then pushed the host into swap exhaustion, and the graphical session crashed after a 92-minute warning no one saw. This note proposes a host-vitals sampler in marvel that would have flagged the file-event growth weeks earlier, and it costs the daemon no new process: it reads from the `ps` pass `RunMetrics` already runs every 5 s.

Docs only: a design note and its finding. Nothing is built, and no existing behavior changes.

- `docs/design/host-vitals.md` covers:
  - what to sample once a minute: swap, memory pressure, top RSS, the file-event daemon, orphaned CPU, and weekly SSD wear (with a GAP line when smartmontools is absent);
  - outputs: a `host.vitals` bus event, crossings in the events ring, OTel gauges where enabled, and `marvel get vitals`;
  - provisional, diagnostic-only thresholds, re-checked on 2026-11-16;
  - no remediation;
  - independence from director and critic;
  - a table of when each of the recent problems would have fired.
- `_kos/findings/finding-marvel-vdni-host-vitals-sampler.md` holds the code reads behind the cost claim, at `8587651a`.
- The split follows the operator's direction: marvel samples, director consumes (director#470 moves from sampling to consuming), and critic trends.
- Section 9 records director's ruling on timing: build before the rc, off unless the cluster config enables it, and enabled on the three fleet hosts. It fits the release party's vote because it adds no always-on loop. The operator may overrule.

Builds on `docs/design/host-health-guard.md` (#1166), section 4.1. Relates to #1214 (samples are never written to bolt) and #805 (the orphaned tmux clients).

## Problem

On Windows, when `grok` resolves to a `.cmd` shim, T3 spawns Grok's ACP process with `shell: true` and `detached: true`. The detached `cmd.exe` gets its own console, `grok.exe` inherits that console instead of T3's stdio pipes, `initialize` times out after 20 s on every provider health check ("ACP initialize failed"), and a blank console window opens each time. Grok sessions use the same spawn path. The reporter's spawn matrix isolates it to `shell: true` + `detached: true`.

## Change

`AcpSessionRuntime` no longer passes `detached: true` when the host is `win32`. `ownDetachedProcessGroup` stays true for Grok, so Windows tree cleanup still runs: it already goes by PID (`taskkill /PID … /T /F`) and never needed a detached group. With `detached` off, Effect's spawner defaults `windowsHide` to true, which also stops the console window. POSIX spawns are unchanged.

## Scope and approval

Fixes pingdotgg/t3code#29088

## Verification

- New test `AcpSessionRuntime > does not detach an owned ACP process tree on Windows hosts` (`apps/server/src/provider/acp/AcpJsonRpcConnection.test.ts`) provides `HostProcess.Platform = "win32"` and records the spawn options. With main's `AcpSessionRuntime.ts`:
